family: net-snmp
what: poll
transport: v3
address: 192.0.2.10
verification: tested
reference: net-snmp manual pages: snmpd.conf(5) (agentAddress, rocommunity, rocommunity6, createUser, rouser)
does: Lets Woodshed poll this machine's snmpd (SNMPv3, read-only).
check: Devices → Add polling → Test poll answers with this machine's name and interfaces; after the first cycle the device page shows its graphs.
placeholders: <V3-USER> <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- Then add this machine in Woodshed: Devices → Add polling, its address, port 161, SNMPv3 and the user <V3-USER>; Test poll shows what answers.
- Add the same user in Woodshed first: Settings → SNMP → v3 users, name <V3-USER>, SHA-256 and AES-128, with the same passphrases (at least 8 characters each).
- Some distributions want createUser in snmpd's persistent file (often /var/lib/snmp/snmpd.conf) instead, written while snmpd is stopped; their net-snmp-create-v3-user tool does that.
- agentAddress replaces snmpd's default listening address; keep any other agentAddress entries you need on the same line, comma-separated.
- Keep snmpd.conf readable by root only: it holds the passphrases.
---- part file "/etc/snmp/snmpd.conf": Add to the agent's configuration, then restart snmpd (sudo systemctl restart snmpd)
# Woodshed: answer polls (SNMPv3, read-only).
agentAddress udp:161,udp6:161
createUser <V3-USER> SHA-256 <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> AES <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
rouser <V3-USER> priv
==== text
